<title>SWITZERLAND: Sulzer sells unit to SHB Schmidlin.</title>
<headline>Sulzer sells unit to SHB Schmidlin.</headline>
<dateline>WINTERTHUR, Switzerland 1997-06-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Technology company Sulzer AG said it sold its Schachenmann &amp; Co AG subsidiary to SHB Schmidlin AG of Basle.</p>
<p>Sulzer said the transaction was retroactive to January 1997, but it gave no financial details.</p>
<p>Schachenmann is involved in electrical installation, planning and switching station construction.</p>
<p>It employs 130 workers and had 1996 turnover of 13 million Swiss francs, Sulzer said. -- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
